	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9249"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402" title="View the profile of Callon">Callon</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 311<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/opus.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Warpig<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=402"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:murgen21@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg9249#msg9249"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg9249#msg9249">Re: (No topic kinda pointless yet redundant topic)</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #5 on:</b> July 12, 2004, 05:27:55 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Both candidates suck.&nbsp; Another crappy ass presidential election... bah.&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/badhairday.gif" alt="badhairday" border="0" /><br /><br />And they&#039;re both SKULLS!!!&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/devil1.gif" alt="Devil" border="0" /> Bastages!&nbsp; <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">He voted agaisnt getting the military better items by voting no to a 86 billion dollar fund for the millitary.&nbsp; </div><br />I agree with a lot of your long post, but... someone could vote against this one strictly for financial reasons.&nbsp; I like some of the things Bush does, but he&#039;s a fiscal moron.&nbsp; He just plain doesn&#039;t give a damn about the debt he&#039;s giving us for the future and those of us early in our careers now as well as kids still in school will be the ones who get to pay for it.&nbsp; National debt is bad when the percentage of the US budget going to pay interest on the debt rises.&nbsp; That&#039;s money that could have been spent on real projects instead of interest.&nbsp; At the record rates Bush is piling up deficits, the percentage paid to debt interest will rise sharply in the coming years.&nbsp; Yet he just keeps on spending like there&#039;s no end to it.<br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg9254"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=317" title="View the profile of Vanden RN">Vanden RN</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Hill Giant<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 179<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=317"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg9254#msg9254"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg9254#msg9254">Re: (No topic kinda pointless yet redundant topic)</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> July 13, 2004, 05:44:32 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Yet he just keeps on spending like there&#039;s no end to it.</div><br />What else can we expect from a politician?&nbsp; I think it&#039;s going to take a relatively average blue-collar type personality getting in the whitehouse to ever try and actually cut the bureaucracy.&nbsp; That or someone who doesn&#039;t give a flip about the longevity of their party in the short run.&nbsp; They&#039;ll be hated by many, not to mention 9/10ths of the lobbyists.&nbsp; Some minor party leaders and independents come to mind, but the majority of American&#039;s avoid them like the plague.&nbsp; All a modern day Republican or Democrat is going to do is create a platform to run on.&nbsp; When they&#039;re in the Oval Office, I bet we won&#039;t see much bureaucracy being cut.<br /><br />Regardless what people think about which class benefits most, in long term Bush&#039;s tax cuts should work out better than not having tax cuts.&nbsp; That&#039;s about all I see going for him on the fiscal side.&nbsp; If only it worked well in the short term also.<br /><br />On another hand though, all this spending, and he&#039;s relatively conservative.<br />In the hands of an even bigger government-builder, Imagine what this <b><i>could</i></b> have been...<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">On that same note you blame Bush for not being able to capture Bin Laden where ever he is hiding, But Bill clinton had him delivered to him on a siliver platter but a few countries and didn&#039;t do anything about it.&nbsp; So who is to blame about 9-11 Bill Clinton,&nbsp; He could have taken Bin laden and 9-11 would have never happened. </div><br />I agree I would have liked us to take that chance when we could, but blaming 9-11 on Clinton, or any particular person for that matter is mostly political expediency.&nbsp; It&#039;s not right.&nbsp; Doing that is kind of like what the media and investigations are doing to the administration and intelligence services.&nbsp; (I&#039;m referring to the terrorist knowledge... putting two and two together.&nbsp; Not the Iraq info)&nbsp; 20-20 hindsight must be a beautiful, addicting gift.&nbsp; Remember, the terrorist attacks must have been set up far far in advance.&nbsp; And with all the planning that went on for it, who&#039;s to say it wasn&#039;t started prior to when Clinton had his chance?&nbsp; And that it would not have still been carried out if he was caught/killed?&nbsp; And if that happened, the stories would be &quot;The terrorists attacked us in retaliation for nabbing Bin Laden&quot; and more organizations would join their cause (and countries may have then said we certainly had it coming).&nbsp; It&#039;s a no win situation and trying to pin blame on people we don&#039;t like or agree with just makes people look... well, like someone else who always used to post his outlandish political opinions on another forum <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /><br /><br />That&#039;s my little run&nbsp; <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cool.gif" alt="Cool" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
