								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg10401#msg10401">Re: (No topic kinda pointless yet redundant topic)</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #8 on:</b> August 24, 2004, 06:48:00 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Good luck voting.&nbsp; Both of them are idiots and there doesn&#039;t seem to be any middle ground.<br /><br />When I was in the U.S. I supported Bush because my husband was in the military.&nbsp; You would not believe the number of military families who are below the poverty line struggling.&nbsp; The pay was sub par, the equipment ancient.<br /><br />Having said that, Bush goes against everything else I hold close to my heart.&nbsp; A woman&#039;s right to chose for herself, the right for any person to get married, etc etc.<br /><br />Luckily I am a Canadian, and we have our own idiots to handle.&nbsp; I just thank God the biggest scandal we&#039;ve had with a Prime Minister had to do with an intruder and Mme Chretien scaring off the man with an Inuit soapstone sculpture.&nbsp; Go go RCMP!<br /><br />And I hope we are never subjected to Mr. Martin sticking his tongue down his wife&#039;s throat like we saw with Mr. Gore.&nbsp; &nbsp;<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/cwm13.gif" alt="cwm13" border="0" />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
