								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=317"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg10432#msg10432"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=912.msg10432#msg10432">Re: (No topic kinda pointless yet redundant topic)</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> August 25, 2004, 05:34:00 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">As for John Kerry&#039;s waffling on issues, i think that it is better to have politicians who are flexible and adaptable, rather than one who has hardcore convictions.</div><br />Last I heard, &quot;waffler&quot; doesn&#039;t simply mean &quot;opinion changer&quot;, but your ideal is still a good one to a point.&nbsp; So let&#039;s find someone who is adaptable and flexible as opposed to someone who waffles depending on which constituency group he&#039;s standing in front of...
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
